From 73e25e5d5b68f9504760cc63bc8f018402668e5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <root@your.mom>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:11:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fuse prompt ranks into selected-score kernels

Upstream base: bb5573c200131b963a1fca31d118de1a9c79e18c. Rationale: remove the separate prompt rank scan/launch in addition to result concatenations. Reuse the existing rank and log-softmax bodies so normal score paths keep their arithmetic, and count ranks with exact integer additions. Quality: preserve selected IDs, score order, NaN/infinity behavior and native ID strides. Tests: all four prompt modes and bitwise comparison against independent kernels for three logits types and both ID widths, including NaN/infinity; GPU compilation, two-boot qualification and default-program identity checks pending. Upstream status: local experiment, not submitted.
